  "status_text": "A contributor reported a 25-gate design for one eight-by-eight graph in the public discussion. The desk opened the question, and Lean accepted a circuit of at most 25 AND and OR gates for it (L-meta-25903). Whether 24 suffice is still open (L-meta-20239, a conjecture). The same hour Lean accepted floors for 134 listed graphs at once: for each of those graphs on eight points, no circuit of AND, OR and NOT gates, each reading at most two wires, detects an edge with fewer than its stated 9 to 13 gates (L-meta-7595).",
